@startuml
!include style.puml
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 170

participant ":EqmManager" as Manager
participant ":LoanHandler" as Handler
participant ":EquipmentHandler" as Inventory
participant "loan:Loan" as Loan
participant "LoanReturnStorage" as Store <<utility>>
participant "item:Equipment" as Item

Manager -> Handler: returnLoan(input)
activate Handler
note over Handler, Inventory
Parse LoanReturn; find a unique active loan and current item.
Check object identity, active loan ID and permanent record ID.
end note
Handler -> Inventory: prepareReturnAssessment(...)
Inventory --> Handler: detached assessed item
Handler -> Loan: returnedCopy()
Loan --> Handler: detached returned loan
Handler -> Store: save(...)
activate Store
note over Store
Save proposals across the equipment,
loan and sequence files.
See ReturnSaveFailure for failure handling.
end note
Store --> Handler: saved successfully
deactivate Store
Handler -> Item: applyReturnAssessment(assessed)
Handler -> Loan: setReturned(true)
activate Loan
Loan -> Item: setLoanId(null)
note over Loan, Item
Clears the active loan flag.
Serviceability still controls availability.
end note
deactivate Loan
Handler --> Manager: original loan, now returned
deactivate Handler
note over Loan, Item
Original objects and permanent IDs are retained.
The loan count and next loan ID do not change.
end note
@enduml
